#: ../../source/fun_project/05-fun_Motion_triggered_relay.rst:18
msgid "Motion triggered relay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/05-fun_Motion_triggered_relay.rst:27
msgid "This Arduino project aims to control a relay-operated light using a passive infrared (PIR) sensor. When the PIR sensor detects motion, the relay is activated, turning the light on. The light remains on for 5 seconds after the last detected motion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/05-fun_Motion_triggered_relay.rst:30
msgid "As a demonstration, we are using a relay to control an RGB LED module. However, in real-life scenarios, this may not be the most practical approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/05-fun_Motion_triggered_relay.rst:32
msgid "**While you can connect the relay to other appliances in actual applications, extreme caution is required when dealing with HIGH AC voltage. Improper or incorrect use can lead to severe injury or even death. Therefore, it is intended for people who are familiar with and knowledgeable about HIGH AC voltage. Always prioritize safety.**"
msgstr ""

